60
00:02:24,733 --> 00:02:25,567
Commercial sign on.

61
00:02:25,567 --> 00:02:26,400
- Amen.

62
00:02:27,333 --> 00:02:30,333
(upbeat techno-pop)

63
00:02:33,033 --> 00:02:34,633
- Come on, we have
to pray for them.

64
00:02:34,633 --> 00:02:35,700
If we could pray for them,

65
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:37,067
we can pray for anybody.

66
00:02:37,067 --> 00:02:39,033
- I don't want to pray
for the mad scientists.

67
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:41,167
- Yeah, Joel, why do we
have to pray for them?

68
00:02:41,167 --> 00:02:42,967
- Well, I think
they're watching,

69
00:02:42,967 --> 00:02:45,067
and they control my oxygen.

70
00:02:45,067 --> 00:02:46,900
- We don't want
you to pray for us.

71
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:48,333
We want you to pray to us.

72
00:02:48,333 --> 00:02:49,200
Isn't that right, Frank?

73
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:51,600
- Don't look at me!

74
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:53,200
I said never look at me!

75
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,500
Mommy, Mommy, ah!

76
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:55,500
- Frank!

77
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:56,967
Calm down!

78
00:02:56,967 --> 00:02:59,567
It's time for the invention
exchange again, Joel,

79
00:02:59,567 --> 00:03:02,900
and we'll go first because we've
got a party to go to later.

80
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:05,367
Well, this summer's
fashions cry out

81
00:03:05,367 --> 00:03:08,333
with jubilant two-inch
armor plating.

82
00:03:08,333 --> 00:03:11,733
Saucy turrets and
shells aplenty.

83
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:13,333
Can really clear the beaches

84
00:03:13,333 --> 00:03:15,600
this summer with
our new tank tops.

85
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:16,667
- That's right.

86
00:03:16,667 --> 00:03:18,267
The best beach party ever

87
00:03:18,267 --> 00:03:20,133
was the one at Normandy.

88
00:03:20,133 --> 00:03:21,767
Beach Blanket Bingo...

89
00:03:21,767 --> 00:03:23,367
(goofy noises)

90
00:03:23,367 --> 00:03:24,833
Is now Beach Blanket Bombing

91
00:03:24,833 --> 00:03:27,033
with the latest in
fashion artillery.

92
00:03:27,033 --> 00:03:28,800
- That's right,
shelling on the beach

93
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,600
takes on a whole new meaning.

94
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:33,633
Let's get in position, Frank.

95
00:03:33,633 --> 00:03:34,733
Ready...

96
00:03:34,733 --> 00:03:35,567
Aim...

97
00:03:35,567 --> 00:03:36,400
Fire.

98
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:40,633
(shot fired)

99
00:03:40,633 --> 00:03:42,600
Now, let's see how we've done.

100
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:44,100
- Hey, wait a minute.

101
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:45,733
I can hear the war.

102
00:03:45,733 --> 00:03:47,300
- Oh, knock that off.

103
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:48,133
- Oh, oh.

104
00:03:48,133 --> 00:03:49,867
- Now, look at here.

105
00:03:49,867 --> 00:03:51,600
Look, there's
still a little red.

106
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:53,000
I'm sorry, I can't
give you the bear.

107
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,800
- Damn, why?

108
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,633
- Well, what do you think, Joel?

109
00:03:56,633 --> 00:04:00,467
- Boy, we sure think
differently, thank
goodness, you know.

110
00:04:00,467 --> 00:04:03,033
You know, you guys took
something fun and made it evil

111
00:04:03,033 --> 00:04:05,900
whereas I took something evil

112
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:07,367
and I'm making it fun.

113
00:04:07,367 --> 00:04:09,333
Check it out, it's the
Tickle Bazooka, all right?

114
00:04:09,333 --> 00:04:13,067
It's for those times
when just a normal tickle

115
00:04:13,067 --> 00:04:14,500
isn't enough.

116
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:16,067
I based it on the premise
of what the pundits

117
00:04:16,067 --> 00:04:17,867
Fire sign Theater once spoke.

118
00:04:17,867 --> 00:04:19,867
Fightin's out of style.

119
00:04:19,867 --> 00:04:21,567
Fun's where the fear is.

120
00:04:21,567 --> 00:04:24,233
See it's got a feather bayonet

121
00:04:24,233 --> 00:04:26,167
